--TEST--
No clause may name a `Core` class: not a class's `extends` or `implements`, not an interface's `extends`, and not an exception class under `Core` — `rule:core-api/core-classes-are-sealed`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A `Core` method reads its receiver's data by position, so a subclass
// written here would give it data it never wrote.
class Forged extends Core\Test\Response {
    public string $note = "x";
}

class Pretend implements Core\Http\Response {
}

interface Wider extends Core\Test\Outcome {
}

// The exception classes under `Core` are thrown by `Core` alone.
class MyDbError extends Core\Db\DbError {
}

// An imported name is the same class.
use Core\Time\Date;
class Birthday extends Date {
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0329]: `Core\Test\Response` is a `Core` class, and your code cannot extend it
%a
error[E0329]: `Core\Http\Response` is a `Core` class, and your code cannot implement it
%a
error[E0329]: `Core\Test\Outcome` is a `Core` class, and your code cannot extend it
%a
error[E0329]: `Core\Db\DbError` is a `Core` class, and your code cannot extend it
%a
error[E0329]: `Core\Time\Date` is a `Core` class, and your code cannot extend it
